actors as candidate 0 (≈ 1.10 and ≈ 1.05).\n- **Gain.** It orders on 14 days instead of 27, so it pays 350 instead of 675, saving 325.\n- **Cost.** It holds about half a day's demand extra each night, roughly 36 units × 0.3 × 25 days ≈ 275.\n- **Net.** That is about +50 compared with candidate 0. Pooling two days of demand into one batch also slightly reduces shortages.\n- **Capacity.** The tightest morning is day 17, at about 223 of 240 units on average, so overflow is rare. Cash is never a constraint.\n\n**3. Candidate 1 (orders every 3 days).**\n- **Gain.** It pays 225 in fixed fees, saving about 450 versus daily ordering.\n- **Cost.** It holds about a full day's demand extra each night, roughly 550 in storage. Its net result is worse than daily ordering.\n- **Capacity.** It also hits the 240-unit limit. On day 17 the forecast stock is about 252, so the extra units are lost. It runs close to the limit again on day 20.\n- **Risk.** Three-day batches are more exposed to random demand, through shortages late in the cycle and spoilage.\n\n**Result:** candidate 2 is ahead, with candidate 0 next and close behind."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3836, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3836}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-25T19:13:40.548Z", "request_id": "req_011CgPVB2XFTK5vRGCkbZg1t"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_0111Z2UUxAsx5x82jqAJBeGX", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "