ead of the best daily plan.\n- With 4-day shelf life, a 2-day batch still has 2 days of slack, so write-off risk barely rises.\n- The highest stock is about 210 units, under the 240 capacity, so nothing is lost on arrival.\n- There is enough cash at every order.\n\n**Candidate 1 (every 3 days, 9 orders, fees 225).** It saves about 450 in fees, but holding a full extra day of demand costs about 525. It also nearly fills the warehouse: around day 22, about 168 units of product 0 arrive on top of roughly 80 already in stock, so some arriving goods could be lost. A 3-day batch with 4-day shelf life is also more exposed to write-offs when demand is low.\n\n**Under random demand.** Candidate 2's safety factor sits close to the best balance between shortage and write-off costs. Its 2-day batching keeps a buffer without running into capacity or write-off limits. So it is also the most robust when actual demand moves away from the forecast."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 357, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5749, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 357}, "output_tokens": 6, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-25T19:13:40.700Z", "request_id": "req_011CgPVCFJxmiJ2pyftPeeiK"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_017KNMhBqATcEqt4kptx8qp1", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgPVCFbLBG1c9SjPGg65E", "type": "message", "role